    std::meta::info _;
    consteval auto f() const {}
} a {};

consteval {
    std::meta::reflect_constant(&a);
}

int main() {}
```
std::meta::reflect_constant(&a) is rejected only when the object's type contains both a consteval-only data member (e.g. std::meta::info) and a non-static consteval member function. Removing either member makes the program well-formed. GCC accepts all variants.
