**Describe the bug**

The following code fails to compile
```
#include <print>
#include <meta>

template<typename ...Types>
struct S{
    struct inside_S;
    consteval {
        define_aggregate(^^inside_S, {
        data_member_spec(^^int, {.name="a"}),
        data_member_spec(^^char,{.name="b"}),
        data_member_spec(^^double,{.name="c"}),
        });
    }
};

int main(){

    using for_template = S<int,float,double>;
    auto lambda = []<for_template V>()
    {

    };

    lambda.template operator()<for_template{}>();

}

```
with the rather intriguing error message `'inside_S' cannot be defined in a parameter type`


Known workaround:
Make inner type templated

```
template<typename ...Types>
struct S{
    template<typename ...Ts>
    struct inside_S;
    consteval {
        define_aggregate(^^inside_S<Types...>, {
        data_member_spec(^^int,{.name="a"}),
        data_member_spec(^^char,{.name="b"}),
        data_member_spec(^^double,{.name="c"}),
        });
    }
};
```



**To Reproduce**
https://godbolt.org/z/z3YnY9fo4



**Additional context**
GCC manages to compile the example code

